-- title:
--   Classify-preimage of j(mathsf q^{qd}) specialises to cyclic-quotient j
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$; $\ell_g$ is a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. the image of $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$ is assumed, by `hW`, to consist of exactly the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)` (the supersingular places), and $s$ is an element of $W$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of intermediate fields of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, where the left side is the base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field and the right side the $X_H$-function field for level $q^2M'$ and $H =$ `levelH q M'`. Next, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` — that is, a valuation subring of integers in the source field, a surjective residue map onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, compatibility with $A$ and with orders of elements, and the existence of scalings with nonzero residue — and `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   A second group of hypotheses concerns a small field of definition. Here $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ has image in $A$; writing $A_0$ for the valuation subring `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`, it is assumed that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), that $A_0$ is a henselian local ring (`hhens`), that its residue field is algebraically closed (`hres`), and (`hκ`) that every $a \in A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   Roots of unity and level: $\xi \in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell_g$-th root of unity (`hξ`), and `hιξ` provides a ring homomorphism $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ carrying $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell_g))$. The subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ is (`hH₁`) the intersection of `levelH q M'` with the kernel of the reduction map to $(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$. The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $k_0 \subseteq$ `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` equal (`hK`) to the base change to $k_0$ of `xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`, carrying an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with $k_0$, and $j \in K$ is the element whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq`, assumed nonzero.
--
--   Three equivariance hypotheses are imposed for all $A_0$-algebras $T$: `hℓ`, that `IsGamma1Point W ℓg D` is preserved by a Weierstrass variable change $C$ acting simultaneously on $W$ and on the level-$p$ datum $D$; `hM`, that `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` is preserved on replacing $h$ by `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`; and `hL`, that divisibility $h \mid$ `inLineMulPoly W ℓg n x` transports to `kernelVariableChangeDeg C d h` dividing `inLineMulPoly (C • W) ℓg n (u⁻¹² (x - r))`.
--
--   The Drinfeld-level data consist of group laws $\mathcal G$ on projective Weierstrass models over $A_0$-algebras, assumed chord-tangent (`h𝒢`) and with the origin as identity section (`h𝒢O`); a level transport $\mathcal T$ for $\mathcal G$ and $q$, assumed to be a section transport (`h𝒯`); together with `hVC` and `hCO`, which provide, for every $A_0$-algebra $T$ and every projective Weierstrass curve over it, graded ring homomorphisms realising a variable change, respectively a coefficient change along an $A_0$-algebra map, with the irrelevant ideal condition needed for the induced map on `Proj`.
--
--   Finally, $P_0$ is a `LevelModuliPackageAbs` over $A_0$ for the level moduli datum of `rigidDataH1Pow ↥A₀ ℓg M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯`: an $A_0$-algebra $B_0 =$ `P₀.B₀` with a universal point `P₀.univ` such that every point with values in an $A_0$-algebra $T$ is the image of the universal one under a unique $A_0$-algebra map. A point $x_0$ of this datum with values in $K$ is given whose $j$-invariant is `jqNModC ↥k₀ q` (`hx₀`), and $\mathrm{cl}_C$ is an $A_0$-algebra map from $B_0$ to the finite chart subalgebra `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin ↥A₀ ↥K j` which, after inclusion into $K$, agrees with `P₀.classify x₀` (`hclC`).
--
--   The hypothesis `hμ` pins $x_0$ to the Tate curve. It asserts the existence of a Weierstrass variable change $C$ over `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` and of a raw representative $r$ of $x_0$ such that: the class of $r$ is $x_0$; writing $(x,y)$ for `tateToricPoint ↥k₀ q` evaluated at the unit $\xi^{q}$, one has $u\,(2x + 1/6) = 2y + x$ for $u = C.u$, and $C.r = -1/12$, $C.s = -1/2$, $C.t = 1/24$ as constant Laurent series; the curve of $r$, pushed to `LaurentSeries ↥k₀`, equals $C \bullet$ `tateBase ↥k₀ q`; for every prime $p$ dividing $M'$, every field $F'$ with a ring homomorphism $f$ from $k_0$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta \in F'$, the $p$-component polynomial `r.level.1 p`, pushed to `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` and then mapped coefficientwise by $f$, equals the `kernelVariableChangeDeg` transform, along the image of $C$ and in degree `gamma0PowDeg p (M'.factorization p)`, of $\prod_{1 \le a \le p^{v_p(M')}/2,\ p \nmid a} (X - (\,$`toricPoint F' q (ζ ^ a)`$)_1)$; the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-datum `r.level.2.1`, pushed to `LaurentSeries ↥k₀`, equals the variable change by $C$ of the `LevelPData` with coordinates $(x,y,x,y)$ for the same Tate toric point; and there exist $P_x, P_y, Q_x, Q_y \in K$ whose Laurent series are the four coordinates of the variable change by $C$ of `cuspData ↥k₀ q` at $\xi^{\ell_g}$ with vectors $(1,0)$ and $(0,-1)$ in $(\mathbb Z/q)^2$, such that the sections $P$ and $Q$ of the Drinfeld level structure `r.level.2.2` pass through $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ respectively.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is the following. Let $d$ be a nonzero natural number dividing $M'$, assume `jqNModC ↥k₀ (q * d)` lies in $K$, and let $c \in B_0$ satisfy `P₀.classify x₀ c` $=$ `jqNModC ↥k₀ (q * d)` as an element of $K$. Assume in addition the reading hypothesis `hread`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ that is an $A_0$-algebra and a $K$-algebra in a compatible tower, every raw representative $x_\Omega$ whose class is the image of $x_0$ under the induced map from $K$ to $\Omega$, and every point $g$ of the affine curve of $x_\Omega$ such that $g$ has exact additive order $M'$ and, for every prime $p \mid M'$, every $n$ and every nonsingular affine point $(x_1,y_1)$ with $n \cdot g = (x_1,y_1)$ and $n \cdot g$ of order $p^{v_p(M')}$, the polynomial `xΩ.level.1 p` vanishes at $x_1$, the image of `jqNModC ↥k₀ (q * d)` in $\Omega$ equals [`WeierstrassCurve.cyclicQuotientJ (xΩ.curve) (AddSubgroup.zmultiples ((M' / d) • g)) d`](def/WeierstrassCurve_CyclicQuotientJ.html#L144), namely $c_4^3/\Delta$ of the corresponding cyclic quotient curve. Then for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ which is an $A_0$-algebra, every $A_0$-algebra map $\varphi : B_0 \to \Omega$ such that $\varphi$ annihilates every $b'$ with $\mathrm{cl}_C(b') = 0$, with $M' \ne 0$ in $\Omega$, every raw representative $x_\Omega$ whose class is the image of the universal point `P₀.univ` under $\varphi$, and every point $g$ of the affine curve of $x_\Omega$ satisfying the same two conditions (exact order $M'$, and the $x$-coordinates of the relevant multiples being roots of the corresponding $\Gamma_0$-level polynomials), one has
--   $$\varphi(c) = \mathtt{cyclicQuotientJ}\,(x_\Omega.\mathrm{curve})\,\bigl(\langle (M'/d)\cdot g\rangle\bigr)\,d .$$
--   Note that in the conclusion no $K$-algebra structure on $\Omega$ is assumed; only an $A_0$-algebra structure and the vanishing condition on $\varphi$ relative to $\mathrm{cl}_C$.
--
--   This is the specialisation step for the $H_1$-level Drinfeld moduli data: a reading of the modular function `jqNModC ↥k₀ (q * d)` valid over all algebraically closed fields containing $K$ is propagated to arbitrary algebraically closed specialisations of the representing algebra $B_0$, where the value of the chosen preimage $c$ is identified with the $j$-invariant of the quotient of the specialised curve by the cyclic subgroup of order $d$ generated by $(M'/d)\cdot g$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_classify_preimage_forall_apply_eq_cyclicQuotientJ_etale_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_classify_preimage_forall_apply_eq_cyclicQuotientJ_etale_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1), and relies on a Chevalley-type valuation-subring extension, on invariance of the cyclic-quotient $j$-invariant under change of generator and under base change to algebraically closed fields, and on its compatibility with reduction.
